  "instruction": "1. **Workspace**: Skill tool → **superpowers:using-git-worktrees** for an\n   isolated worktree.\n\n2. **Executor**: Skill tool → **superpowers:subagent-driven-development**,\n   executing the slices in tasks.md with a fresh subagent per slice.\n\n   Tell the executor to read tasks.md in this change directory, update its\n   checkboxes as slices complete, and work inside the worktree.\n\n   Transitive — do NOT invoke these manually:\n   - **superpowers:test-driven-development** — RED-GREEN-REFACTOR per slice.\n     Implementation written before a failing test is deleted.\n   - **superpowers:requesting-code-review** — a reviewer subagent after each\n     slice, plus a final review before apply concludes.\n\n   Fallback only where subagents are unavailable: **superpowers:executing-plans**,\n   which does NOT bring TDD or code-review. You then owe both manually.\n\n3. **Debugging**: unexpected failures go through\n   **superpowers:systematic-debugging** before any fix is proposed.\n\n4. **Verification**: produce the `verify` artifact. Re-run until no blocking\n   issues remain. The failure-proof table is not optional.\n\n5. **Completion**: Skill tool → **superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch**.",
  "context": "Read AGENTS.md before producing any artifact. Rules R1-R5 there govern every\nartifact and every line of code. The two that bite hardest:\n\nR5 — Unknown is not OK. Missing file, unreadable state, absent tool, malformed\ntrusted data, unexpected nullish: throw. Never default them away. Every new\nsafety check needs a negative test on its production call path, watched failing\nwith the check removed, and an adjacent `Proof:` comment naming the injected\nfault. Checks that cannot fail have shipped here six times.\n\nR3 — Knowledge about a symbol lives in JSDoc on that symbol. Knowledge that\nspans files lives in docs/ and is linked from the JSDoc. CONTEXT.md is the\ndomain glossary, terms only. docs/adr/ is for decisions that are hard to\nreverse, surprising, and had real alternatives.\n\nStack: Nx monorepo, Bun everywhere, never npm. be-01 (Elysia + Drizzle +\nbun:sqlite, :3100), gw-01 (WS gateway, :3200), fe-01 (Vite + React).\nBlue/green deploy: two be-01 processes share one SQLite file during a swap,\nso migrations must be backward-compatible.\n\nUse CONTEXT.md's terms exactly. If you need a term it lacks, resolve it in the\ndesign interview and add it to CONTEXT.md before using it in an artifact.\n\nCI runs on GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) and is the merge gate:\n`bunx nx format:check --all`, then `bunx nx run-many -t test lint typecheck build`,\nthen `bunx @fission-ai/openspec@1.12.0 validate --all --json`. Locally, gate on h2puni with\n`bin/h2puni-gate.sh`, which takes the host-wide lock; AGENTS.md forbids the\nraw full Nx gate there. The earlier \"there is no CI\" line was stale and\nunder-scoped every plan that inherited it: it omitted format and build.\n",
